        "original_id": "a17bfeb4-d860-5ae7-ace2-05925441d343",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: David Hilbert, André Weil, Serre, Grothendieck\n- Topics: classical algebraic geometry, algebraic geometry terminology, general methods\n- Organizations: Italian school of algebraic geometry\n\nFacts:\n- David Hilbert was a German mathematician who lived from 23 January 1862 to 14 February 1943.\n- At the beginning of the twentieth century, David Hilbert and the Italian school of algebraic geometry initiated general methods in algebraic geometry.\n- During the twentieth century, the terminology of algebraic geometry changed drastically.\n- Later in the twentieth century, André Weil, Serre, and Grothendieck formalized the general methods of algebraic geometry.",
